## Reproducer

```sh
cd ~/work/zen/jxl-encoder
CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$HOME/work/zen/jxl-encoder-shared-target \
  cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder \
    --features 'parallel butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop' \
    --example w44_124_auto_discriminator_ab
```

Build info captured here. TSV columns:
- baseline_off_bytes, auto_default_bytes, keep_dct32_bytes
- baseline_off_bfly, auto_default_bfly, keep_dct32_bfly
- baseline_off_ssim2, auto_default_ssim2, keep_dct32_ssim2
- auto_vs_baseline_off_bytes_pct, auto_vs_baseline_off_ssim2
- auto_vs_keep_dct32_bytes_pct, auto_vs_keep_dct32_ssim2

## DO NOT

- DO NOT lower `W44_124_DCT32_KEEP_M3_MIN` below 60 — imessage sits at
  67.65 with d=6 -0.37 SSIM2 regression, and is the closest non-codec_wiki
  screen. Going below 50 admits imessage which regresses.
- DO NOT raise `W44_124_DCT32_KEEP_EDGE_DENSITY_MAX` above 0.05 — imessage
  sits at 0.0533 and would slip through.
- DO NOT widen the auto-discriminator without re-running the regression
  set (6 SCREEN cells + all 24 photos). The thresholds are validated by
  the W44-124 probe and tight on every side.
- DO NOT remove the W44-65 outer gate — without it, the auto-discriminator
  would fire on non-screenshot content where DCT32X32 vs 4×DCT16X16 has
  not been validated.
